DTSTAMP:20260902T060828Z
SUMMARY:INSIGHTS IN HISTORY – THE FIRST SETTLERS OF INDIANA
LOCATION:The History Museum | 808 W Washington St | South Bend\, 46601
DESCRIPTION:In conjunction with our exhibit First Peoples\, First Settlers:
  Indiana’s Interwoven Roots\, Exhibits Coordinator Emily Demler will te
 ll the story of the first European settlers to come to Indiana\, focusing
  on influential figures like Pierre Navarre\, Alexis Coquillard\, and oth
 ers. A tour of the exhibit will be offered after the talk.\n\nRegister to
 day at https://historymuseumsb.app.ne...\n\nMore Info: https://www.visits
 outhbend.com/events/insights-in-history-the-first-settlers-of-indiana/
URL:https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/insights-in-history-the-first-set
 tlers-of-indiana/
